From ec986a1f13d7388f7efbebc28568f0cac7cddc9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Avis <jonathanavis96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:34:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Disable thinking and trim TYPE_TEXT context for the
 standing text model

MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=0 (env var, no CLI flag exists) removes the extended-
thinking cost that dominated latency on the standing child and the per-call
adapter alike, with no correctness change on the cases tested. A trimmed
element-table context (chosen field + 5 nearest rows + page title/url, no
page body text) replaces the full page-text context by default, selectable
via TEXT_MODEL_CONTEXT=full|trimmed; correctness verified on Wikipedia
search, an origin/destination flights disambiguation, a date field and an
email field.

Stacked, these take TEXT_MODEL_PROVIDER=claude-standing from the previously
measured regression (11.0-12.6s wall, 6.55s fill) to the fastest configuration
in this repo (7.5s wall, 739ms fill for the README Wikipedia goal), beating
the per-call claude-cli adapter this spike had settled on as the floor.

See SPIKE-NOTES.md "Thinking off and trimmed context" for full measurements.
